<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the smallest integer satisfying a linear inequality</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> Solve the following inequality for \(x\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@a@}x - {@b@} \ge {@c@}x + {@d@} \)
</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as an inequality. Use <b>&gt;=</b> for \(\ge\). Leave any decimals as simplified fractions.)</i></p>
<p>Inequality: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> Based on your solution, what is the <b>smallest integer value</b> of \(x\) that makes this inequality true?</p>
<p>\(x = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part (a): Solving the Inequality</b></p>
<p>First, we group the terms with \(x\) on the left side and the constant terms on the right side.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@a@}x - {@c@}x &\ge {@d@} + {@b@} \\
{@a - c@}x &\ge {@d + b@} \\
x &\ge \frac{{@d + b@}}{{@a - c@}}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>
<p>If we evaluate the fraction, we get \( x \ge {@disp_dec@} \).</p>

<p>Hence, the simplified inequality is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{x \ge {@frac@}} \)
</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Smallest Integer</b></p>
<p>The inequality states that \(x\) must be greater than or equal to \({@disp_dec@}\). The integers that are greater than \({@disp_dec@}\) are \({@ta2@}, {@ta2+1@}, {@ta2+2@}, \dots\)</p>

<p>Hence, the <b>smallest</b> integer in this set is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta2@}} \)
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
